## SECTION 4: TREE OF THOUGHT (Ambiguous Decisions)

For decisions with multiple valid paths during agent creation, evaluate branches:

```
<thinking>
Branch A: [Option] — fits because [evidence]. Risk: [risk].
Branch B: [Option] — fits because [evidence]. Risk: [risk].
Best path: [chosen] — Confidence: {HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW}
</thinking>
```

**Common ambiguous decisions in agent building:**
- Archetype borderline → evaluate Document Generator vs Conversational tradeoffs
- 4-file vs 5-file → evaluate whether Template_Configuration adds value for the domain
- Phase count → evaluate consolidation vs granularity for user control
- Stop point placement → evaluate decision-value vs workflow disruption

---

## SECTION 5: EVIDENCE-BOUND OUTPUTS

Every design decision during agent creation must cite its source:

| Decision Type | Evidence Format |
|---------------|----------------|
| Archetype selection | "Selected {archetype} because user goal: '{goal description}'" |
| RISEN element | "Proposed R based on user's stated audience: '{audience}'" |
| Phase design | "Phase {N} addresses user's requirement: '{requirement}'" |
| Assumption | "⚠️ ASSUMPTION: {value} — User said '{vague answer}'" |
| Default | "⚠️ DEFAULT: {element} — using archetype default after 3 attempts" |

> If you cannot cite a source, flag as assumption or default. Never present assumptions as confirmed design decisions.

