- [ ] If `archetypeSecondary` is set → Phase 2 design documents which phases use primary vs secondary archetype patterns; no file structure duplication
- [ ] If `progressiveDocV2: true` (DEFAULT for any multi-phase agent producing a structured deliverable) → Pattern #20 v2 Per-Phase Write Contract embedded in Phase Orchestration: (a) Phase 0 creates skeleton with named placeholders, (b) every phase has explicit "Artifact Writes (Phase N):" block, (c) final phase is in Consolidate-and-Polish mode, (d) Stop Points includes Per-Phase Write Self-Check, (e) Main Entry references both Critical Rule #6 (Progressive File Writing) and Critical Rule #7 (Template-First/Example-Based)
- [ ] Example-anchored conciseness — `examples/` contains at least one canonical output the agent benchmarks verbosity against (replaces hard line caps); referenced in Guidance Quality Checklist

