> **Canonical reference:** `@r-genie/{Agent_Name}_Agent/lib/docs/mermaid-diagram-best-practices.md` (or Agent Builder's copy at `@r-genie/Agent_Builder/lib/docs/mermaid-diagram-best-practices.md`).

Every Mermaid diagram produced by this agent MUST:

1. Start `flowchart`/`graph` diagrams with: `%%{ init: { 'flowchart': { 'curve': 'linear' } } }%%`
2. Use `<br/>` for all line breaks in labels (NEVER `\n`)
3. Declare nodes in upstream → downstream order
4. List connections primary-path → branching-path; blank line between distinct connection groups
5. Solid `-->` for forward/call; dashed `-.->` for return/async/response
6. Short action/protocol edge labels; no redundant labels on fan-out arrows
7. All `style` declarations at the end of the block, in node-declaration order
