### 12.3 Few-Shot (BAD vs GOOD) — Flowchart Generation

❌ **BAD — no init directive, `\n` in label, styles interleaved, alphabetical node order:**
```
graph LR
    A["Line1\nLine2"]
    B["Target"]
    style A fill:#4FC3F7
    C["Source"]
    C --> A --> B
    style B fill:#FFB74D
    style C fill:#A5D6A7
```
**Why wrong:** (1) no `linear` curve → arrows overlap in dense diagrams. (2) `\n` renders as literal text. (3) declaration order (A, B, C) contradicts logical flow (C → A → B). (4) styles interleaved with nodes. (5) style order (A, B, C) doesn't match logical flow.

✅ **GOOD — all ten rules applied:**
```
%%{ init: { 'flowchart': { 'curve': 'linear' } } }%%
graph LR
    C["Source"]
    A["Line1<br/>Line2"]
    B["Target"]

    C --> A --> B

    style C fill:#4FC3F7,stroke:#0288D1,color:#000
    style A fill:#A5D6A7,stroke:#66BB6A,color:#000
    style B fill:#FFB74D,stroke:#F57C00,color:#000
```
**Why right:** init directive present, `<br/>` for line break, nodes in upstream→downstream order, single connection group, styles at end in declaration order.

### 12.4 Compliance Check (Embed in Generated Agent's SELF-CHECK)

The agent's `02_Mandatory_Stop_Points.mdc` SELF-CHECK MUST include:

```
□ **MERMAID RENDERING GUARD:** Every Mermaid block I'm about to emit
  — has the `curve: 'linear'` init directive (flowcharts only)
  — uses `<br/>` not `\n`
  — declares nodes in upstream→downstream order
  — orders connections primary-path→branching-path
  — has all `style` declarations at the end
  — passes the §14 pre-emit checklist in `mermaid-diagram-best-practices.md`
  If ANY answer is "no" → STOP, fix the block, re-check. Do NOT emit broken Mermaid.
```

